# Exercises `actor {} <: Principal` across an actor-class upgrade: a stable var
# typed `actor {}` in v0 migrates into a `Principal`-typed var in v1.
#
# Runs on BOTH backends. Classical re-serialises the stable record through Candid
# (stabilize/destabilize), so the old `service`-encoded value reads back as a
# `principal` — the representation coincides, so it round-trips. EOP does not
# re-serialise; it gates the upgrade with the RTS `memory_compatible` check
# (idl.rs, a Candid-subtyping checker over the serialized type table), which now
# carries the `service <: principal` case (mirroring the Motoko type rule and the
# Candid spec extension), so the in-place reinterpretation is accepted. Both
# backends print `aaaaa-aa` before and after the upgrade.
install $ID actor-sub-principal-stable/version0.mo ""
ingress $ID show "DIDL\x00\x00"
upgrade $ID actor-sub-principal-stable/version1.mo ""
ingress $ID show "DIDL\x00\x00"
